# Every text file checks out with LF, on Windows too (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true).
# World Packs are YAML: a CRLF inside a block scalar would change a string, then a fact, then AC-8's
# Windows record (docs/DECISIONS.md ARC-49; step-14 §13.10.1 W-3).
* text=auto eol=lf
# The one file committed with CRLF keeps its bytes: it is a third party's licence text, never renormalized.
clients/3d-spike/assets/characters/LICENSE.quaternius-ual.txt -text

# glTF binary buffers and GLB containers are binary data. Git's own test (a NUL byte in
# the first 8000 bytes) misses some of them: bar_chair_round_01.bin was diffed as text,
# and a diff with invalid UTF-8 broke the acceptance scan that reads `git diff` output
# (tests/acceptance/tests/precursor_vocabulary.rs).
*.bin binary
*.glb binary
